1
00:00:23,982 --> 00:00:25,650
‎Biochip is secure.

2
00:00:25,734 --> 00:00:27,152
‎What about the punk?

3
00:00:27,235 --> 00:00:28,653
‎He's of no value now.

4
00:00:28,737 --> 00:00:30,071
‎Scrap him.

5
00:01:10,695 --> 00:01:11,738
‎Capri...

6
00:02:50,795 --> 00:02:53,006
‎Hey, Sal. Brought you a reel.

7
00:02:53,965 --> 00:02:55,216
‎Roman.

8
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:58,219
‎This is probably the last one of D.

9
00:02:58,887 --> 00:03:01,431
‎You didn't go?

10
00:03:01,514 --> 00:03:03,391
‎-Go where?
‎-You haven't heard?

11
00:03:06,686 --> 00:03:10,273
‎The riots in Heywood have been dispersed.

12
00:03:10,982 --> 00:03:13,359
‎While the suspected
‎instigator remains at large,

13
00:03:13,443 --> 00:03:16,029
‎all other threats have been neutralized.

14
00:03:16,112 --> 00:03:19,741
‎Travel conditions in the district
‎are expected to return to normal shortly.

15
00:03:24,162 --> 00:03:25,622
‎Who's there?

16
00:03:27,916 --> 00:03:28,917
‎Talia.

17
00:03:30,209 --> 00:03:31,252
‎Where've you been?

18
00:03:33,546 --> 00:03:34,672
‎Weak?

19
00:03:36,466 --> 00:03:37,467
‎I'm sorry.

20
00:04:07,372 --> 00:04:08,373
‎Weak?

21
00:04:10,583 --> 00:04:11,876
‎Miss Yang?

22
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:14,712
‎Found the Yangs' daughter.
‎She's in the morgue now.

23
00:04:16,422 --> 00:04:18,466
‎No, I haven't asked her yet.

24
00:04:38,444 --> 00:04:40,238
‎Wait, where's the body?

25
00:04:40,321 --> 00:04:42,490
‎-We've disposed of it.
‎-Disposed of it?

26
00:04:43,074 --> 00:04:45,243
‎Our orders were to get the chip...

27
00:04:45,910 --> 00:04:47,161
‎You killed him?

28
00:04:48,579 --> 00:04:51,499
‎Fucking morons! Idiots! Worthless trash!

29
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:55,461
‎His body's worth more
‎than a thousand of you!

30
00:05:01,384 --> 00:05:02,844
‎-Die.
‎-Kyoko, enough!

31
00:05:03,386 --> 00:05:05,054
‎Who fucked up the orders?!

32
00:05:05,138 --> 00:05:06,723
‎This is on you!

33
00:05:08,141 --> 00:05:10,560
‎Only the chip? Where's the boy?

34
00:05:10,643 --> 00:05:12,312
‎Says they scrapped him!

35
00:05:12,812 --> 00:05:15,523
‎This is why Kang Tao
‎will always be second-rate.

36
00:05:15,606 --> 00:05:16,607
‎Militech would never have let--

37
00:05:18,985 --> 00:05:20,653
‎Will that suffice?

38
00:05:21,404 --> 00:05:22,947
‎Now check the chip if you please.

39
00:05:35,835 --> 00:05:37,503
‎Eat this!

40
00:05:37,587 --> 00:05:39,964
‎-Fuck!
‎-Can ya hear me?

41
00:05:40,048 --> 00:05:41,340
‎Let's go, chooms.

42
00:05:49,182 --> 00:05:50,224
‎Don't.

43
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:52,226
‎Don't touch her.

44
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:54,479
‎Please be reasonable.

45
00:05:54,562 --> 00:05:58,024
‎I said no. My dad's not even here yet.

46
00:05:58,107 --> 00:06:00,234
‎We've got his sign-off already.

47
00:06:00,318 --> 00:06:02,445
‎Then where the hell is he?!

48
00:06:03,154 --> 00:06:04,363
‎I'm sorry.

49
00:06:04,447 --> 00:06:06,074
‎The fuck does that mean?!

50
00:06:06,157 --> 00:06:08,826
‎Stop! You're not burning my mom!

51
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:10,119
‎Dammit!

52
00:06:10,203 --> 00:06:12,371
‎You know I'd help right now if I could.

53
00:06:15,416 --> 00:06:16,459
‎Mom!

54
00:06:41,109 --> 00:06:43,903
‎How'd it get to this...

55
00:06:50,952 --> 00:06:52,829
‎Imagine you're sitting
‎on a pile o' eddies.

56
00:06:52,912 --> 00:06:56,624
‎No wait, a room full of eddies.
‎A swimming pool.

57
00:06:56,707 --> 00:06:59,585
‎-‎A football stadium!
‎-So, what's the plan now?

58
00:07:02,964 --> 00:07:06,300
‎Can't believe you caused
‎a riot against Arasaka.

59
00:07:06,384 --> 00:07:07,593
‎Are you stupid?

60
00:07:09,637 --> 00:07:13,599
‎It's only safe to crash here
‎one night, tops. Is that clear?

61
00:07:14,517 --> 00:07:17,979
‎I greased the receptionist,
‎but it won't hold.

62
00:07:31,701 --> 00:07:35,913
‎What did you want to accomplish?
‎Revenge this, revenge that...

63
00:07:36,581 --> 00:07:38,583
‎You keep this up, it's gonna kill you.

64
00:07:38,666 --> 00:07:40,084
‎That what you want?

65
00:07:50,887 --> 00:07:53,973
‎Sorry to bother.
‎I'm calling about Ms. Talia Yang...

66
00:07:55,683 --> 00:07:56,934
‎"Blank"?

67
00:07:57,018 --> 00:07:59,687
‎-What do you mean "blank?"
‎-Shut up.

68
00:07:59,770 --> 00:08:02,607
‎Her soul's gone missing!
‎It's not on the damn chip!

69
00:08:03,107 --> 00:08:05,693
‎Fuck! It's just a piece of junk!

70
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:08,321
‎It must have some power still. Perhaps--

71
00:08:08,404 --> 00:08:09,697
‎Use your brain for a second!

72
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:13,075
‎That's a brakeless car doing
‎a hundred on the highway.

73
00:08:13,159 --> 00:08:15,203
‎And we don't even have a body it fits!

74
00:08:15,286 --> 00:08:17,705
‎Damn it! How did he...

75
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:23,920
‎Think... He looked like shit,
‎but he was still clearly himself.

76
00:08:24,462 --> 00:08:28,424
‎And he didn't seem to be talking
‎with any voices in his head.

77
00:08:29,133 --> 00:08:32,553
‎Installs don't take that long, anyway.

78
00:08:33,221 --> 00:08:34,514
‎Which means...

79
00:08:36,974 --> 00:08:38,726
‎Did she split somewhere?

80
00:08:44,815 --> 00:08:45,900
‎Kyoko?

81
00:08:45,983 --> 00:08:48,069
‎Yes, yes, Kyoko here.

82
00:08:48,152 --> 00:08:49,695
‎You OK? It looked bad...

83
00:08:50,947 --> 00:08:53,491
‎Ah! That was nothing...

84
00:08:53,574 --> 00:08:57,578
‎A little rattled of course.
‎How kind of you to worry about me.

85
00:08:57,662 --> 00:08:58,746
‎That's good...

86
00:08:59,497 --> 00:09:01,624
‎D was actin' strange, real strange.

87
00:09:01,707 --> 00:09:02,833
‎But uh...

88
00:09:02,917 --> 00:09:05,753
‎Y'know you kinda were too... seemed off.

89
00:09:05,836 --> 00:09:08,923
‎Rattled, as I said.

90
00:09:09,006 --> 00:09:11,008
‎Now, I'd like to talk to you about D.

91
00:09:12,260 --> 00:09:14,554
‎The boy may not seem himself,

92
00:09:14,637 --> 00:09:17,348
‎but... he doesn't seem
‎cyberpsychotic either.

93
00:09:17,431 --> 00:09:19,892
‎-In my expert opinion.
‎-Really?

94
00:09:20,518 --> 00:09:24,355
‎That shard in his neck...
‎It's no normal chip.

95
00:09:25,147 --> 00:09:28,150
‎It must be a prototype
‎or something of the kind.

96
00:09:28,818 --> 00:09:31,654
‎When he first inserted it...
‎his troubles started right then?

97
00:09:32,613 --> 00:09:33,781
‎Guess so.

98
00:09:33,864 --> 00:09:36,951
‎Whatever you know of the shard, tell me.

99
00:09:37,535 --> 00:09:39,370
‎You might be the key to helping him.

100
00:09:40,454 --> 00:09:44,750
‎This one time...he slotted
‎the shard into a girl. A choom of mine.

101
00:09:44,834 --> 00:09:48,337
‎He what?! He put the chip in someone else?

102
00:09:48,421 --> 00:09:52,008
‎Why would he do that?

103
00:09:52,091 --> 00:09:54,260
‎To remove it, give it away,
‎take it back? Why?

104
00:09:54,343 --> 00:09:55,803
‎What happened to her?

105
00:09:56,554 --> 00:09:58,014
‎Knocked her out,

106
00:09:58,097 --> 00:10:01,475
‎sent her to the hospital. She couldn't
‎really move or do anything after.

107
00:10:01,559 --> 00:10:03,436
‎She's OK now, I think...

108
00:10:03,519 --> 00:10:05,438
‎Seemed bad, but bounced back.

109
00:10:06,188 --> 00:10:07,398
‎She recovered?

110
00:10:09,317 --> 00:10:11,694
‎Hey, Kyoko? Do you know something?

111
00:10:11,777 --> 00:10:13,571
‎Again, you're saying she's healthy?

112
00:10:13,654 --> 00:10:17,658
‎Yeah, kinda. Stable, at least.
‎Still at the hospital.

113
00:10:17,742 --> 00:10:19,201
‎Which hospital?

114
00:10:19,285 --> 00:10:23,205
‎Kyoko, why the sudden interest?
‎What's she matter to you?

115
00:10:23,789 --> 00:10:26,626
‎Problem's D. He's off-grid.
‎Saw the feeds yourself.

116
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:28,919
‎-‎What is this shard?
‎-Sorry. Call you back.

117
00:10:33,507 --> 00:10:37,303
‎No doubt about it. That must've been
‎the moment Capri's engram split!

118
00:10:38,179 --> 00:10:39,388
‎It can't be...

119
00:10:39,472 --> 00:10:40,806
‎What? What is it?

120
00:11:00,534 --> 00:11:01,535
‎Talia.

121
00:11:02,453 --> 00:11:04,664
‎How did Mom die?

122
00:11:05,956 --> 00:11:06,957
‎I'm sorry.

123
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:09,752
‎That's what you're here
‎to tell me, isn't it?

124
00:11:10,503 --> 00:11:12,880
‎Don't tell me you came
‎all this way just to check on me.

125
00:11:14,256 --> 00:11:15,257
‎Yeah.

126
00:11:19,678 --> 00:11:23,015
‎Your mom and I broke into
‎a Kang Tao research facility.

127
00:11:23,891 --> 00:11:27,186
‎We got caught at the end.
‎During the escape, Avida was shot.

128
00:11:28,354 --> 00:11:30,940
‎By the time we reached
‎the hospital... She was already...

129
00:11:31,899 --> 00:11:33,401
‎Why would she do that?

130
00:11:34,110 --> 00:11:36,862
‎We were gonna find you another body.

131
00:11:37,863 --> 00:11:39,990
‎...A body? For me?

132
00:11:40,658 --> 00:11:44,412
‎The thought being, if we could
‎transfer your soul into a new one...

133
00:11:44,495 --> 00:11:46,247
‎you'd get a second chance.

134
00:11:47,415 --> 00:11:48,874
‎My soul?

135
00:11:48,958 --> 00:11:50,668
‎Tech called Soulkiller.

136
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:55,089
‎Arasaka developed it,
‎and Kang Tao's got their own copy.

137
00:11:56,132 --> 00:12:00,052
‎The facility we broke into was
‎where they kept the bodies meant for it.

138
00:12:01,387 --> 00:12:02,972
‎You were really gonna do that?

139
00:12:03,597 --> 00:12:05,099
‎You and Mom?

140
00:12:05,933 --> 00:12:08,352
‎We wanted to save you.

141
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:11,814
‎Who asked you to?

142
00:12:13,357 --> 00:12:15,818
‎What made you think I would want that?

143
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:20,698
‎It weighed on your mom until the very end.

144
00:12:22,741 --> 00:12:24,243
‎This is bullshit.

145
00:12:24,910 --> 00:12:26,787
‎This is bullshit!

146
00:12:43,596 --> 00:12:46,265
‎Talia. You seem to be doing well.

147
00:12:46,932 --> 00:12:49,310
‎Dad. You're a little late.

148
00:12:50,019 --> 00:12:51,645
‎They already put Mom in a jar.

149
00:12:52,730 --> 00:12:55,274
‎She died trying to save me!

150
00:12:55,357 --> 00:12:56,775
‎You bastard--

151
00:12:58,027 --> 00:12:59,487
‎Talia! He was there!

152
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:02,364
‎At the facility, commanding the unit!

153
00:13:03,699 --> 00:13:07,119
‎He knew Avida was there
‎and opened fire anyway!

154
00:13:07,786 --> 00:13:09,079
‎Please put a muzzle on him.

155
00:13:13,626 --> 00:13:15,503
‎Dammit, let me go!

156
00:13:19,924 --> 00:13:21,133
‎Come with me.

157
00:13:21,842 --> 00:13:23,761
‎Did you shoot Mom?

158
00:13:23,844 --> 00:13:25,304
‎That's ridiculous.

159
00:13:25,387 --> 00:13:28,849
‎I was there! You killed Avida!

160
00:13:28,933 --> 00:13:30,559
‎Why can I still hear him?

161
00:13:32,603 --> 00:13:34,772
‎-Go.
‎-Answer him!

162
00:13:34,855 --> 00:13:37,608
‎Don't touch me! Lemme go!

163
00:13:37,691 --> 00:13:40,653
‎Capri! Do something!

164
00:13:41,195 --> 00:13:42,780
‎Don't...

165
00:13:43,656 --> 00:13:46,033
‎Don't you lay a hand on my daughter.

166
00:13:46,116 --> 00:13:48,619
‎Sorry? What're you raving about?

167
00:13:48,702 --> 00:13:50,079
‎Think I misheard.

168
00:13:50,162 --> 00:13:53,707
‎Avida told me. Talia's my daughter.

169
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,253
‎There it is.

170
00:13:57,336 --> 00:13:59,463
‎Is that what Avida said?

171
00:13:59,547 --> 00:14:02,132
‎It all makes sense now.

172
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:13,060
‎You miserable fool. Look here.

173
00:14:14,645 --> 00:14:18,732
‎Proof. Talia is mine
‎by every imaginable measure.

174
00:14:27,533 --> 00:14:31,287
‎Genes! Bloodline! Bone structure!

175
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:34,665
‎Everything says she's mine!

176
00:14:35,624 --> 00:14:38,544
‎Talia is ‎my‎ daughter!

177
00:14:51,015 --> 00:14:53,100
‎You could've checked yourself.

178
00:14:53,183 --> 00:14:56,312
‎Just one simple test would
‎have proved it beyond any doubt.

179
00:14:58,689 --> 00:15:00,691
‎But you were eager to buy her story.

180
00:15:01,901 --> 00:15:04,695
‎Because deep down you feared the truth.

181
00:15:05,404 --> 00:15:07,197
‎She's my daughter.

182
00:15:17,291 --> 00:15:21,795
‎Talia is my daughter!

183
00:15:27,217 --> 00:15:31,138
‎Dad? Did you kill Mom?

184
00:15:32,264 --> 00:15:33,849
‎A pointless question.

185
00:16:06,215 --> 00:16:07,216
‎Avida...

186
00:16:08,676 --> 00:16:13,889
‎That means if you purchase it
‎with standard armor-plating,

187
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:17,351
‎this British sports-limo is safer than
‎a tank, and, as I'm sure you'd agree,

188
00:16:17,434 --> 00:16:18,602
‎offers far more panache.

189
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:22,231
‎This is a side of you I don't recognize.

190
00:16:25,818 --> 00:16:29,905
‎Remember? You saved me, once.

191
00:16:30,531 --> 00:16:31,532
‎Back when we...

192
00:16:34,868 --> 00:16:38,622
‎They're all gone.

193
00:16:38,706 --> 00:16:39,790
‎What?

194
00:16:40,541 --> 00:16:42,376
‎The people that hit our clan...

195
00:16:43,043 --> 00:16:44,795
‎The suit that ordered it...

196
00:16:45,421 --> 00:16:46,880
‎They're all dead.

197
00:16:48,757 --> 00:16:51,135
‎And not a single thing
‎I did fuckin' mattered.

198
00:16:52,011 --> 00:16:53,012
‎Oh...

199
00:16:54,805 --> 00:16:56,348
‎What was I supposed to do?

200
00:17:05,733 --> 00:17:09,111
‎Hmm... I see...

201
00:17:09,194 --> 00:17:10,654
‎Hmm...

202
00:17:14,158 --> 00:17:17,494
‎Hey, are these electromagnets
‎in her arms and legs?

203
00:17:17,578 --> 00:17:18,620
‎Will it work or not?

204
00:17:18,704 --> 00:17:22,166
‎These for motion-assist?
‎Were you training her for the circus?

205
00:17:23,751 --> 00:17:26,879
‎Whoa, relax. Just asking...

206
00:17:28,797 --> 00:17:30,924
‎Girl's really sick, isn't she?

207
00:17:31,550 --> 00:17:35,054
‎We slowed the illness by replacing
‎her failing tissue with cyberware.

208
00:17:35,971 --> 00:17:38,348
‎Believing she possessed
‎a special tolerance to it...

209
00:17:38,932 --> 00:17:40,309
‎She does.

210
00:17:40,392 --> 00:17:43,228
‎Saw her on an Arasaka list.

211
00:17:43,896 --> 00:17:45,731
‎Flagged as a host candidate for Capricorn.

212
00:17:46,523 --> 00:17:47,566
‎Did they now?

213
00:17:47,649 --> 00:17:52,488
‎Of course, she was too risky to go after,
‎being the kid of a rival corp exec.

214
00:17:53,238 --> 00:17:55,240
‎But... will this still work?

215
00:17:55,324 --> 00:17:56,325
‎In what sense?

216
00:17:56,992 --> 00:17:59,995
‎Her tolerance
‎has already reached its limit,

217
00:18:00,621 --> 00:18:02,456
‎pushing her to the brink
‎of cyberpsychosis.

218
00:18:03,123 --> 00:18:05,250
‎On top of that,
‎the illness has spread to her brain.

219
00:18:05,334 --> 00:18:07,836
‎The doctors say
‎she doesn't have long to live.

220
00:18:08,712 --> 00:18:11,507
‎Say the install succeeds, but Talia dies...

221
00:18:12,132 --> 00:18:14,093
‎what happens to Capricorn?

222
00:18:15,594 --> 00:18:16,595
‎What?

223
00:18:17,221 --> 00:18:19,848
‎Which one are you worried about?

224
00:18:21,433 --> 00:18:22,810
‎It's fine.

225
00:18:22,893 --> 00:18:24,978
‎There's some brain damage, sure.

226
00:18:25,062 --> 00:18:30,734
‎But Capricorn's already begun repairing
‎some of it during the installation.

227
00:18:31,693 --> 00:18:34,696
‎Full installation should
‎allow for further recovery.

228
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:37,950
‎But the process will overwrite
‎the host's native consciousness,

229
00:18:38,033 --> 00:18:39,827
‎and she'll disappear.

230
00:18:40,994 --> 00:18:41,995
‎I see.

231
00:18:42,579 --> 00:18:43,872
‎So I have your go-ahead?

232
00:18:44,915 --> 00:18:48,919
‎You can begin. As I said,
‎she has little time left anyway.

233
00:18:49,002 --> 00:18:52,172
‎Good. Spoken like a true corpo.

234
00:19:04,643 --> 00:19:05,769
‎Hey.

235
00:19:07,062 --> 00:19:08,272
‎Capri.

236
00:19:08,981 --> 00:19:12,025
‎Sorry, but you gotta go bye-bye now.

237
00:19:12,609 --> 00:19:15,404
‎Well, I guess technically...
‎you'll become me.

238
00:19:16,363 --> 00:19:17,656
‎I see.

239
00:19:17,739 --> 00:19:21,451
‎That's it?
‎You really are a strange cookie.

240
00:19:23,245 --> 00:19:24,580
‎Don't you have any regrets?

241
00:19:25,956 --> 00:19:27,791
‎It's not like I don't, but...

242
00:19:35,841 --> 00:19:37,759
‎...Mm. Actually...

243
00:19:38,510 --> 00:19:40,429
‎Will you kill him for me?

244
00:19:41,221 --> 00:19:42,806
‎As gruesome as you can.

245
00:19:43,974 --> 00:19:45,559
‎For my mom.

246
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:48,687
‎Okay.

247
00:19:55,277 --> 00:19:56,737
‎Oh, hey Kyoko...

248
00:20:09,041 --> 00:20:10,125
‎Mmm. That's better.

249
00:20:10,792 --> 00:20:13,212
‎Is it safe to remove her restraints?

250
00:20:13,295 --> 00:20:15,005
‎-I didn't do that.
‎-What?

251
00:20:15,881 --> 00:20:17,883
‎Thanks, Kyoko.

252
00:20:21,470 --> 00:20:24,181
‎I can finally do whatever I want.

253
00:20:24,264 --> 00:20:26,934
‎You shouldn't be up. Sit back down.

254
00:20:32,814 --> 00:20:33,815
‎Restrain her!

255
00:20:43,700 --> 00:20:47,246
‎I was asked to make this
‎as gruesome as possible.

256
00:20:47,329 --> 00:20:50,249
‎But that doesn't mean
‎it can't be fun, too, right?

257
00:20:50,332 --> 00:20:52,542
‎I'll give you a 3-minute head start.
‎Better start running.

258
00:20:52,626 --> 00:20:53,919
‎Daddy.

259
00:20:56,421 --> 00:20:57,547
‎That's enough!

260
00:21:06,139 --> 00:21:09,059
‎You really thought this would stop me?

261
00:21:11,937 --> 00:21:13,063
‎There, gave ya a handicap!

262
00:21:13,146 --> 00:21:15,065
‎Fuck! What's wrong with you?!

263
00:21:15,148 --> 00:21:19,486
‎Aw nuts, think I gave ya
‎the wrong kind of handicap!

264
00:21:19,569 --> 00:21:20,570
‎Sorry, sorry!

265
00:21:20,654 --> 00:21:21,738
‎What're you--

266
00:21:25,534 --> 00:21:27,452
‎Commencing countdown!

267
00:21:28,453 --> 00:21:32,332
‎Ten... Nine... Eight...

268
00:21:34,418 --> 00:21:35,585
‎Capri!

269
00:21:37,754 --> 00:21:39,089
‎You're alive.

270
00:21:39,756 --> 00:21:42,259
‎Is it... done?

271
00:21:43,218 --> 00:21:44,428
‎Is the installation complete?

272
00:21:46,179 --> 00:21:50,475
‎Why's everyone so obsessed
‎with revenge, anyway?

273
00:21:51,810 --> 00:21:55,230
‎Is revenge, like, fun?

274
00:21:55,314 --> 00:21:56,732
‎What are you...

275
00:21:57,858 --> 00:21:59,693
‎Wait! Capri!

276
00:22:23,592 --> 00:22:25,886
‎The subject has escaped.

277
00:22:25,969 --> 00:22:28,597
‎Deploy a team to find
‎and secure her immediately!

278
00:22:29,139 --> 00:22:31,641
‎Escaped? What are you talking about?

279
00:22:31,725 --> 00:22:33,643
‎You'll get a full report later!

280
00:22:33,727 --> 00:22:35,520
‎Just get a damn team moving!

281
00:22:36,354 --> 00:22:38,648
‎Move them where? And... wait.

282
00:22:40,358 --> 00:22:41,818
‎What is it?

283
00:22:41,902 --> 00:22:43,487
‎I can see you.

284
00:22:59,002 --> 00:23:00,003
‎What is this?

285
00:23:01,129 --> 00:23:03,632
‎Just hurry!

286
00:23:03,715 --> 00:23:05,550
‎Shit!

287
00:23:07,135 --> 00:23:10,639
‎C'mon, put a little pep in your step!

288
00:23:11,139 --> 00:23:12,182
‎Shit!

289
00:23:12,265 --> 00:23:14,935
‎There you go! Keep it moving!

290
00:23:22,400 --> 00:23:23,401
‎Talia?

291
00:23:26,655 --> 00:23:31,451
‎Hey. You asked yesterday
‎what you were supposed to do.

292
00:23:33,286 --> 00:23:35,622
‎It doesn't matter.

293
00:23:35,705 --> 00:23:38,125
‎You could'a done anything.

294
00:23:39,126 --> 00:23:42,838
‎The past, the present... it doesn't matter.
‎You should'a done what you wanted, David.

295
00:23:57,018 --> 00:23:58,019
‎Capri.

296
00:24:06,319 --> 00:24:07,445
‎Who's this?

297
00:24:07,529 --> 00:24:09,781
‎Directive received to capture Capricorn.

298
00:24:10,490 --> 00:24:14,077
‎Team arriving shortly. Maintain heading.
‎Proceed straight down the street.

299
00:24:14,161 --> 00:24:15,162
‎Understood.

300
00:24:25,130 --> 00:24:27,632
‎Done already?

301
00:24:51,740 --> 00:24:54,034
‎Hey! Where do you think you're going?!

302
00:24:55,243 --> 00:24:56,870
‎Gonna go find Capri.

303
00:24:56,953 --> 00:24:58,997
‎Capri? Who or what is that?

304
00:25:02,500 --> 00:25:03,752
‎This is the last time, Omi.

305
00:25:05,837 --> 00:25:08,173
‎This is the end of the line.

306
00:25:10,926 --> 00:25:12,260
‎Lend me a hand.

307
00:25:12,928 --> 00:25:14,512
‎I can't do this on my own.

308
00:25:22,103 --> 00:25:23,939
‎You're not making any sense.

309
00:25:24,022 --> 00:25:25,982
‎Ow! What was that for?!

310
00:25:26,566 --> 00:25:31,446
‎I don't understand any of it.
‎But... fine. I'll help.

311
00:25:31,529 --> 00:25:33,615
‎Just let me change first.

312
00:25:40,038 --> 00:25:43,959
‎Ugh, this is getting boring.

313
00:25:45,543 --> 00:25:47,629
‎Time to wrap it up.

314
00:27:19,888 --> 00:27:24,893
‎Subtitle translation by:
‎CD PROJEKT RED & Megumi Hunter
